  "details": "Use machine translation\n\n# VRChat Version: 1345\n\n# SDK Version: 3.3.0\n\n# Description of the bug:\n\nWhen launching 3 or more clients in Offline Test, each client after the third one is in a different instance.\n\nDisplayed in 3D space and confirmed from Udon's PlayerId\n\nPlayerId:\n\n1st client:1\n\nSecond client: 2\n\n3rd client:1\n\n4th client:1\n\n# Steps to reproduce (how did you encounter the bug?):\n\n1. open VRChat's World project in Unity\n\n2. In the SDK's Builder tab, in the Offline Testing field, set the Number of Clients to 4.\n\n3. Press \"Build & Testing New Build\n\n4. Confirm that there is only one or two players in the same instance (world).\n\n# Any extra files? (output logs, screenshots):\n\n# --\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/sdk-bug-reports/p/sdk862-offline-test-option-is-broken-with-multiple-clients\n\nThis may be included in the URL above, but I am unable to debug the synchronization properly.\n\nIf this seems to be a problem, please fix it.",
